+## 38.00 startup test
+
+Use the latest **Emilyfn-Memory-Capture-Windows-x64** artifact and extract the
+whole ZIP. The 38.00 diagnostic profile requires the exact supplied CL47722112
+executable inside its complete matching installation; it does not enable 38.00
+in the normal Play workflow.
+
+1. Close the previous game instance.
+2. Open **Logs → Game diagnostics → Launch 38.00 diagnostic** and select
+   `FortniteGame/Binaries/Win64/FortniteClient-Win64-Shipping.exe`.
+3. Wait about 30 seconds. The newly started process is selected automatically.
+4. Select **Test 38.00 game-thread dispatch**, choose a report folder, and share
+   the small `dispatch-test.json` file.
+
+The diagnostic launch passes the game's built-in `-SkipPatchCheck` option and
+saves a small launch report. This tests whether that option advances startup;
+it is not a verified fix for the early content-patcher wait. The JSON reports
+patch completion, progress, active-screen identity and whether the option was
+observed in the game's command line. It never exports the command line itself.
+No full memory dump is needed for this test. Close the diagnostic game manually
+when finished; it is separate from the normal Play session lifecycle.
+
+If this launch exits immediately, its report includes the observed exit code;
+**Capture 38.00 startup** remains available for a full early-exit trace. The
+binding/dispatch checks still decline function calls without a verified target.
+Full 38.00 lobby/gameplay, server hooks, LEGO Fortnite and Festival remain unfinished.
